{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deliver","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"destinations","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","text":"Destination","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"..., ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchBufferLimit","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 100) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsynchronousUnitOfWorkP","text":"AsynchronousUnitOfWork","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<()>\n","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"destinations","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Where each batch goes.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"batchBufferLimit","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"How many batches each destination may have waiting while it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still receiving an earlier one."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A unit of work that completes once the last batch is delivered, and throws what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the sequence throws, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"type":"text","text":" when cancelled."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(to: ConsoleDestination(), vendor)","try await delivery.execute()"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each destination receives its batches in order, one at a time, from a buffer of its own,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a slow destination delays only itself. When a batch arrives while a destination’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"buffer already holds "},{"code":"batchBufferLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" batches, the oldest waiting batch is dropped."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Once the sequence ends, the work completes after every destination has received its last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store keeps (those with an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord.deliveryTag"},{"type":"text","text":") are reported to it:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before a batch goes to any destination, and again once every destination’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has returned for it without being cancelled, when the store may forget them. A record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the store couldn’t mark as being delivered is left out of the batch, and a batch left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no records isn’t sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Records the delivery has read but not delivered are lost to this run when it is cancelled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or fails, and so are batches a destination’s full buffer dropped. Without a store they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gone; a store never had them acknowledged, so it delivers them on the next launch (unless","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its bound drops them first, which it reports).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing runs until the work is executed, and each execution reads the sequence again, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a delivery that finished or failed can be executed again (a retry). Cancelling it drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the batches its destinations had waiting, and is permanent, as for every Afluent unit of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"work: executing a cancelled delivery again throws "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at once, so build a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new one instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batchBufferLimit"},{"text":" is at least 1.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The work of delivering each batch of this sequence to every destination, until the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence ends.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations\/_concurrency\/asyncsequence\/deliver(to:batchbufferlimit:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)","modules":[{"name":"Destinations","relatedModules":["_Concurrency"]}],"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"deliver"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"kind":"text","text":": any "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Destination"},{"kind"